\fs28 WAVsToALE (Windows) — Readme\par
\fs24 Version 1.0.1\par
\par
\b Overview\b0\par
WAVsToALE generates Avid ALE files from WAV metadata (BEXT, LIST-INFO, embedded XML). It can automatically infer UCS category/subcategory when no UCS ID prefix is present in the filename.\par
\par
\b Quick Start\b0\par
1) Run \b WAVsToALE.exe\b0\par
2) Choose input WAVs or a folder, and an output directory\par
3) (Optional) Check “Infer UCS category/subcategory if filename lacks a UCS ID”\par
4) Click Run; find ALE outputs in your chosen location\par
\par
\b UCS Inference (Best‑Guess)\b0\par
When filenames lack a UCS ID prefix, the app infers category/subcategory by scoring text from:\par
- Filename words\par
- BEXT Description\par
- LIST-INFO fields\par
- Embedded XML text (when present)\par
\par
\b How scoring works (concise)\b0\par
- Normalize text (lowercase, strip punctuation, split to words)\par
- Score each UCS entry using:\par
  • Whole-word overlaps with the UCS Subcategory (highest weight)\par
  • Keyword/synonym overlaps from the UCS list (medium weight)\par
  • Partial string matches on the Subcategory (lower weight, 3+ chars)\par
- Pick the top score; record alternatives and flag “low confidence” for weak matches\par
\par
\b Notes\b0\par
- ALE format unchanged; only matching behavior improved\par
- Backward-compatible CLI flags: --ucs-inference / --no-ucs-inference\par
